<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Holdfast Bay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Holdfast Bay is a bay on the eastern shore of Gulf St Vincent in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, now lined by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide">Adelaide</a> suburbs of Glenelg and Brighton. Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hindmarsh">John Hindmarsh</a> proclaimed the Province of South Australia there on 28 December 1836, a date still marked each year as Proclamation Day. The Old Gum Tree at Glenelg North marks the traditional site of the ceremony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holdfast-bay.jpg" alt="Holdfast Bay" width="320" height="150" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was AtD (Adam Trevorrow) at en.wikipedia · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GlenelgBeach.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
